---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import InfoPage from '../components/InfoPage.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, GITHUB_ISSUES_URL } from '../consts';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — Poimi';
const description =
	'Privacy policy for Poimi, the iOS app for hand-picking photos into an album. On-device, no account, no tracking.';
---

<MarketingLayout title={title} description={description} noindex>
	<Nav />
	<InfoPage
		kicker="Poimi"
		title="Privacy Policy"
		updated="Draft — pending sign-off"
	>
		<p>
			Poimi is an on-device iPhone and iPad app for hand-picking your photos
			into an album in Apple Photos. It does not run ads, does not use
			third-party analytics, and does not upload your photos. The publisher and
			data controller is <strong>Valtteri Luoma</strong> (contact:
			<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>).
		</p>

		<h2>The short version</h2>
		<p>
			Poimi processes your photos entirely on your device. It does not upload,
			transmit, or store your photos anywhere. There is no account and no
			tracking. Poimi is free, with no purchases &mdash; so there is no payment
			data.
		</p>

		<h2>What Poimi accesses</h2>
		<p>
			Poimi requests <strong>Full Access</strong> to your photo library &mdash; required
			so it can read a whole date range, remember your selections across sessions,
			and write the finished album back (Apple&rsquo;s Limited Access / Selected Photos
			cannot do these). Poimi does <strong>not</strong>
			request location permission; it reads the GPS coordinate already embedded in
			a photo when one is present.
		</p>

		<h2>What is stored, and where</h2>
		<p>
			Only on your device: the identifiers of the photos you picked, your album
			settings (name, date range, target, exclusions), and a local cache of
			place names. Poimi never stores the image or video files themselves.
		</p>

		<h2>Network use — the one exception</h2>
		<p>
			To label trips and places, Poimi sends a photo&rsquo;s coordinate to
			Apple&rsquo;s reverse-geocoding service to get back a human place name.
			This uses Apple&rsquo;s service under Apple&rsquo;s terms; Poimi runs no
			server of its own and keeps no coordinate log. Resulting names are cached
			locally.
		</p>

		<h2>No third parties</h2>
		<p>
			No advertising, analytics, or tracking SDKs; no data is sold or shared. If
			you opt in to sharing diagnostics with developers in iOS Settings, Apple
			may provide aggregate, anonymized crash and usage reports via App Store
			Connect &mdash; Poimi collects nothing else.
		</p>

		<h2>Your control and deletion</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>
				Deleting an album inside Poimi removes only Poimi&rsquo;s record of it;
				your real photos are untouched.
			</li>
			<li>Uninstalling the app removes all of Poimi&rsquo;s local data.</li>
			<li>An exported album is a normal Photos album you manage in Photos.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Questions</h2>
		<p>
			Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> or open an issue
			on the <a href={GITHUB_ISSUES_URL}>GitHub issue tracker</a>.
		</p>
	</InfoPage>
	<Footer />
</MarketingLayout>
